Actually, looking at the target molecule again: `COC(C1(C=C1[Si](C)(C)C)/C=C/C2=CC=CC=C2)=O`

This could be interpreted as a methyl acrylate derivative with a silyl-substituted cyclopropene and phenyl group attached. Perhaps it could be formed by a cyclopropanation reaction of methyl acrylate with a silyl carbene or similar.

But I need a single-step synthesis. Given the complexity, I think the esterification route is the most straightforward, even if the acid precursor might not be commercially available.

